EXPERIMENT: drm/h713-afbd: bisect why a smaller source renders black

A 960x544 source renders BLACK on the panel while 1280x720 renders correctly,
and the difference is not the upscaler: bypassing it mid-run, with the plane
still live, changes nothing.  The fetcher registers are provably right in both
cases -- SIZE_M1 0x021F03BF, BLOCK_M1 0x0021003B, strides 0x3C0, and a chroma
offset of exactly 960*544 -- and the composition block is byte-identical
between the working and failing runs.

So the fault is in getting a smaller source to render at all, and the only
other thing that differs is the VideoInfo descriptor, which 0098 rewrites to
the source geometry while leaving its canonical 1920x1080 crop rectangle
alone.

These knobs exist because iterating on a built-in driver costs a POWER CYCLE
per hypothesis, not a reboot: a warm reboot leaves this display unable to show
anything at all, which cost most of a session to notice.  They are writable at
runtime so one cold boot can test several combinations.

  vi_follow=0   leave the descriptor at its probe geometry
  vi_crop=1     express the crop rectangle in the source's own scale
  proc_en=0     never engage the proc upscaler

Drop this patch once the cause is known.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/sun50i-h713-afbd.c
@@ -190,6 +190,24 @@
 	unsigned int video_info_h;
 };
 
+/*
+ * EXPERIMENT knobs.  A source smaller than the panel renders BLACK even with
+ * the upscaler bypassed, while 1280x720 renders correctly, and the fetcher
+ * registers are provably right in both cases.  These exist to bisect that from
+ * userspace, because every rebuild of a built-in driver costs a power cycle --
+ * a warm reboot leaves the display unable to show anything at all.
+ *
+ *   vi_follow=0   leave the VideoInfo descriptor at its probe geometry
+ *   vi_crop=1     scale the canonical 1/16-pixel crop rect with the source
+ *   proc_en=0     never engage the proc upscaler
+ */
+static int vi_follow = 1;
+module_param(vi_follow, int, 0644);
+static int vi_crop;
+module_param(vi_crop, int, 0644);
+static int proc_en = 1;
+module_param(proc_en, int, 0644);
+
